; The project verdict aliases, once, at the top of the test tree — the
; two workflows windtrap tells its users to adopt, adopted here, plus
; the third that only an alias can ask. All three are opt-in: none is
; attached to @default or @runtest, and a plain `dune runtest` stays
; uninstrumented, zero-overhead and free of coverage and mutation output.
;
;   dune build @cover --instrument-with ppx_windtrap.coverage
;
;   WINDTRAP_MUTATE=1 dune exec --instrument-with ppx_windtrap.mutate \
;     test/unit/test_diff.exe --
;   dune build @mutate
;
; The two are not symmetric, and the asymmetry is the runtimes'. Coverage
; accumulates as a side effect of running: an instrumented suite writes
; its .coverage dump at exit whatever it was asked to do, so one alias
; both runs and merges. A mutation VERDICT only exists if a suite was
; asked to test its mutants — WINDTRAP_MUTATE=1 takes the process over
; and runs the fork loop — so `@mutate` merges what previous runs left
; and, on its own, correctly reports that it found nothing.
;
; Why an alias and not a script: `.coverage` and `.mutants` files are
; written by test executables at exit and are not declarable dependencies,
; so nothing can express "after every suite has run". (alias_rec runtest)
; forces every stanza in the tree up to date first, and (universe) makes
; the milliseconds-cheap aggregate re-run on every build — without it the
; action caches against nothing and silently goes stale. This is the
; shape examples/09-coverage-aggregation documents, one level up.
;
; `ppx_windtrap.coverage` is the backend's one name: it keeps the
; windtrap core out of an instrumented library's closure, which lib/ —
; the core itself — needs to be instrumentable at all. See
; ppx/coverage/dune.

; --min 87 is the measured baseline less a couple of points of headroom,
; not a round number picked in advance. It ratchets: raise it when the
; margin is comfortable, and never lower it to make a red build green.
; Measured 87.5% on 2026-08-19 — the margin is thin because the campaign
; deleted test suites the earlier 89.5% counted, and what is left is
; mostly not reachable: lib/mutate_loop.ml alone is 400 of the ~860
; uncovered points, and structurally so, because its loop body runs only
; under the mutation backend and its children _exit past the at_exit
; dump; mutate_loop's Windows-decline paths and capture's C-stub error
; branches cannot run in a green suite at all. Chase the branches the
; report names, not the percentage — and read mutate_loop's number as
; the report's own blind spot rather than a debt.
;
; ../runtest, not runtest, and the `..` is the whole point: the merge
; reads every .coverage dump under _build, tree-wide, so the run half
; must be tree-wide too. examples/08-coverage, 09-coverage-aggregation
; and x-blueprint each carry an instrumented library, and their points
; are in this report; scoped to test/ the alias would leave them to
; whatever ran last, which is one number locally and another on a fresh
; checkout.

(rule
 (alias cover)
 (deps
  (alias_rec ../runtest)
  (universe))
 (action
  (run %{bin:windtrap} coverage --min 87)))

; Mutation has no gate and deliberately never will (Law 16e): the
; equivalent-mutant rate is a prediction until it is measured, so a
; survivor is a reading list, not a build failure.
;
; Mutate one file at a time — the loop forks once per mutant, and
; WINDTRAP_MUTATE_ONLY narrows the work rather than the report:
;
;   WINDTRAP_MUTATE=1 WINDTRAP_MUTATE_ONLY=lib/diff.ml \
;     dune exec --instrument-with ppx_windtrap.mutate test/unit/test_diff.exe --
;
(rule
 (alias mutate)
 (deps
  (universe))
 (action
  (run %{bin:windtrap} mutate)))

; Admission, the third workflow, and the only one an alias can carry on
; its own. WINDTRAP_MUTATE=admit with no per-invocation selection judges
; every test the run executes, which is the question an alias wants to
; ask and no filter spells. It needs no merging half, because an
; admission run persists nothing (Law 17b) — the rulings it prints are
; the whole product.
;
;   dune build @admit --instrument-with ppx_windtrap.mutate
;
; The flag is required, for @cover's reason: this tree's workspace
; declares no instrumentation, and an uninstrumented executable has an
; empty catalogue, so the seam declines by name instead of ruling.
; --force is not required — (universe) already re-runs the action on
; every build, as it does above.
;
; One rule per unit executable, and one alias over the lot. That is what
; admission costs now that the suite is one executable per module, and
; what it buys: dune runs the rules in parallel where a single
; executable's rulings came out one after another, and a red ruling
; names the executable it came from instead of a position in one
; 570-test transcript. The roster is unit/'s (names ...) list, and a
; test file added there without a rule here is simply not judged — the
; two lists are kept in step by eye, which is the price of dune having
; no way to write this once.
;
; The scope is a statement about what an arming can reach. These are the
; suites whose subject is lib/ — the library that carries the mutation
; backend — exercised in-process, which is the only place a mutant armed
; in this process changes anything. The four meta suites beside them are
; plain executables over the hand-rolled harness, with no windtrap run
; and so no per-test boundary to rule on. The other test directories are
; left out not because admission would be wrong over them but because
; their subject is not lib/'s behaviour: facade, mutate_loop, mutate_cli,
; coverage_ppx, ppx and conformance observe the machinery through
; fixtures they spawn or expansions they diff, so the code under test
; runs where no arming reaches it, and a ruling would name whichever
; fault their own assertion code happened to evaluate — true about the
; test, silent about what the test is for. Widening this is a later
; choice.

(rule
 (alias admit)
 (deps
  (universe)
  unit/test_pp.exe)
 (action
  (setenv WINDTRAP_MUTATE admit (run %{exe:unit/test_pp.exe}))))

(rule
 (alias admit)
 (deps
  (universe)
  unit/test_text.exe)
 (action
  (setenv WINDTRAP_MUTATE admit (run %{exe:unit/test_text.exe}))))

